flowchart LR
    Create["create AF_XDP socket<br/><b>does:</b> binds XSK to ifindex + RX queue + UMEM<br/><b>why next:</b> XDP redirect needs a live socket fd<br/><b>state:</b> socket owns RX/TX rings"]
    Map["update XSKMAP<br/><b>does:</b> stores queue_id -> xsk fd<br/><b>why next:</b> BPF redirect_map looks up by ctx->rx_queue_index<br/><b>state:</b> queue has userspace owner"]
    Packet["packet reaches XDP<br/><b>does:</b> program reads rx_queue_index and policy<br/><b>why next:</b> only registered queues can redirect safely<br/><b>state:</b> xdp_buff still pre-skb"]
    Lookup["bpf_redirect_map<br/><b>does:</b> checks XSKMAP entry for queue<br/><b>why next:</b> hit transfers packet to AF_XDP; miss uses fallback<br/><b>state:</b> redirect target or XDP_PASS"]
    Ring["XSK RX ring<br/><b>does:</b> receives descriptor for UMEM frame<br/><b>why next:</b> userspace polls descriptors, not syscalls per packet<br/><b>state:</b> user owns packet buffer"]
    Cleanup["delete map entry<br/><b>does:</b> removes queue -> fd before socket teardown<br/><b>state:</b> later packets pass/drop instead of targeting stale XSK"]

    Create --> Map --> Packet --> Lookup
    Lookup -->|map hit| Ring --> Cleanup
    Lookup -->|no entry| Pass["XDP_PASS / fallback<br/><b>state:</b> packet continues to normal stack"]

